     "style": "definition",
     "title": "Prefixes and suffixes",
     "md": "A **prefix** is added to the **front** of a word and changes its meaning: **un-** (not): *unhappy*; **re-** (again): *rewrite*; **dis-** (not): *disagree*. A **suffix** is added to the **end**: **-ful** (full of): *helpful*; **-less** (without): *careless*; **-ness** (state): *kindness*; **-ly** makes adverbs: *slowly*."
