     "alt": "A table of prefixes and suffixes: un means not, re means again, dis means not, ful means full of, less means without, ness means state, each with an example."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "retenir",
     "title": "Spelling changes",
     "md": "If a word ends in a **silent e**, drop it before a suffix that starts with a vowel: *hope - hoping*, but keep it before *-ful* and *-ness*: *hopeful*. If a word ends in **consonant + y**, change **y to i**: *happy - happiness, easy - easily*. Double the last letter in short words: *run - running, big - bigger*."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "pieges",
     "title": "Common mistakes",
     "md": "- *Unnecessary* is spelt with *nn* (un + necessary): do not drop a letter.\n- *Carefull* or *usefull*: the suffix is **-ful** with one l.\n- Adding a prefix and changing the spelling of the base word.\n- Confusing *-less* (without) and *-ful* (with)."
